# Response headers for the static pages.
#
# These live here rather than in the Worker because Cloudflare's asset server
# answers HTML before the Worker runs — headers set in worker/index.js never reach
# the pages. Forcing the Worker to run first (run_worker_first) instead sends its own
# ASSETS.fetch back through the same route and 307-loops.
#
# Why they matter beyond hygiene: the member page collects a password and names
# Steam, Google and Apple, which is also exactly the shape of a phishing page.
# Scanners cannot tell the difference from markup alone. form-action pins credential
# submission to this origin, so the page provably cannot post a password anywhere
# else, and base-uri stops an injected <base> from moving it — the behaviour a
# phishing kit needs and this site does not.
#
# Deliberately no script-src / style-src / frame-src: Google Identity,
# appleid.cdn-apple.com, api-merchant.payos.vn and Google Fonts all load
# cross-origin, and a wrong value there breaks sign-in or checkout. Tighten those in
# one deliberate, browser-verified step.
/*
  Content-Security-Policy: form-action 'self'; frame-ancestors 'self'; base-uri 'self'
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=15552000
